# Everything in this repository runs on Linux, so a checkout must be LF no
# matter what the cloning client's core.autocrlf happens to be set to.
#
# This is not a style preference. A CR after "#!/usr/bin/env bash" is not a
# shebang: the kernel looks for an interpreter called "bash\r", fails to find
# it, and the script does not run at all. The same applies to the python3
# shebangs. Checking out on a Windows machine with autocrlf=true - which is
# the Git for Windows default - would do exactly that, so the rule is pinned
# here in the repo rather than left to each clone's configuration.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The reference capture is binary. Line-ending conversion would corrupt it,
# and git's own binary detection is a heuristic rather than a guarantee.
*.wav binary
